s/differential/14041851/assets/1df00f421b20b101d1500b4e2f47054f0c79dcfd2d82585fb8fb3735adb71af5.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=5.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=9?$" :question/worked-solution "The position of the particle at $t=9$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [2,9].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(9)=x(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{9}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(2)=5,$ and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{2}^{9}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=2$ to $t=9.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{9}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(9)=5+2=7.\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=9$ is $x=7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-121021/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "089120d4-b37b-5936-8ea4-b68848290606"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121021"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121014/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "a8162d4f-3175-5cc0-8fcb-2d68bdb61a26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121014/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "a1262e9c-17e1-531c-a52d-655bfc9701fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121014/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "eadce465-34de-5311-9017-91847f2729f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121014/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "18cf1192-fe57-58a9-8a