$ the particle is located at the position $x=-3.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=7?$\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=7$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The position of the particle at $t=7$ is equal to its position at $t=4$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [4,7].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(7)=x(4)+{\\int }_{4}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(4)=-3$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{4}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=4$ to $t=7.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{4}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(7)=-3+3=0.\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=7$ is $x=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-351501/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "089120d4-b37b-5936-8ea4-b68848290606"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351501"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7129"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/assets/900988cb8ec54abcafc256a34c685829d2f5f00cdca373ad84dfa0ef70cc3957.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=-1.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=8?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
